<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="About Nick Nieuwenhuis"
>
	<h2>Enabling organizations to change and innovate securely</h2>

	<p>
		I am a Lead Security Architect at Nedscaper, working at the intersection of cybersecurity strategy, security architecture and cyber risk management.
		My work focuses on translating business objectives, security requirements and organizational risks into practical and scalable security capabilities.

		Coming from a background in business administration, facility management and informatics, my interests extend beyond individual security controls to the architecture behind them:
		how people, processes and technology work together to create resilient organizations that can adapt to change, withstand cyber threats and continue delivering value to their stakeholders.
	</p>

	<p>
		In addition to my professional work, I remain actively involved in academic cybersecurity research, with a particular interest in security architecture, cyber risk management and emerging technologies.

		I collaborate with the Cyber Security lectorate of Utrecht University of Applied Sciences and contribute to the broader academic cybersecurity community.

		My latest publications, presentations and research activities can be found in the Research section of this website.
	</p>

	<p>
		I am also a regular public speaker at conferences, educational events and industry gatherings.

		My speaking engagements primarily focus on cybersecurity architecture, digital resilience and quantum security.

		If you are interested in a keynote, guest lecture, panel discussion or other event, please visit the Speaking section for more information.
	</p>
</Layout>